  "body": "Refs #3319, #3520.\n\n## What happens\nA 2D Offset operation cuts deeper than the flute length of its tool (the search on #3319: `testdata/models/fig8.step`, `EM-0800-4FL` with a flute length of 10 mm, Top 22, Bottom 1.5, Stepdown 10). The shank is wider than the cutter and meets the part on the outer ring of the second and third levels.\n\nThe user gets three `RapidInStock` warnings on vertical rapids at the start of the outer ring. The text says \"travels through stock (below the clearance plane...)\". Nothing names the cause: the cutter is shorter than the cut. The user looked for a lateral rapid that does not exist (#3319).\n\nThe post is blocked in this case. That is correct and does not change.\n\n## Wanted\n- A diagnostic that names the cause before the first rapid finding: the tool, its flute length, and the cut depth that the operation asks for (the depth below the top of the stock at that place).\n- Emit it at the earliest place that has the facts: at generation, or as the first finding of the verifier. A refusal at generation is permitted if the engagement is certain. If it is not certain, give a warning and keep the block of the post.\n- The message is in plain English, with no G-code terms.\n- The post stays blocked while the shank or the holder meets the part or the stock.\n\n## Done when\n- A test reproduces the case of #3319 (flute length 10 mm on `fig8.step` with the heights above) and asserts the new diagnostic with the tool name, the flute length and the depth.\n- A test with a flute length of 25 mm asserts that the diagnostic does not come.\n- The existing collision and rapid findings do not become weaker.\n\n## Notes\n- #3520 corrects the text of `RapidInStock` for a vertical rapid that meets the part. This issue adds the cause.\n- The label is `effort:high`, because the work is in a collision check (AGENTS.md, safety floor).\n",
